Date: Thu, 15 Jul 93 19:50:22 -0700
From: davisd@nimitz.ee.washington.edu
Subject: Scientific validity in metaprogramming experiments 

Dave Krieger makes a number of excellent points about metaprogramming
experiments.

He did gloss over one thing, however. He talked about comparing the
performance of the different groups. It is very important in this study
to follow individual performances and not group means. I think it is 
quite reasonable to think that if these
rituals have any effect at all, they will have different effects for
different people. You might even end up with the same
performance distribution among group A and group B even though the
ritual had a marked performance on the members of Group A, some
positive, some negative.

In short, the relevant statistics are over the changes in each person's
performance, coupled with some estimate of their performance variation in
a sitting, day, week,...

