I am well aware that cancellation can be guaranteed by
symmetry combined with rigidity.  The point at issue is to
achieve cancellation in the absence of symmetry.  There is
no good way to predict cancellation in irregular asymmetric
systems.  I have repeatedly pointed out that once you
rigidly cobble a beautifully symmetric nanocomponent into
a nanomachine, it loses symmetry.

